window.docContents[192].resolve({"/rules/PL1005/#PL1005-trigger":{"contents":"Each declaration receives the least label containing its exact axiom set. If that label exceeds the surface maximum, the declaration is rejected with applicability label-exceeds-claim.\n\nThe three logical labels are Kernel-only (no axioms), Choice-Free (a subset of propext and Quot.sound) and Standard-Logical (additionally Classical.choice). A surface's claim in foundation_manifest.json is the upper bound; each declaration is labeled from its own exact axiom set.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL1005: Transitive axioms must fit the selected profile","header":"What triggers it","id":"/rules/PL1005/#PL1005-trigger"},"/rules/PL2004/#PL2004-trigger":{"contents":"Module inventory comes from Lake's elaborated configuration and Lean's recorded module indices, not from file lists or name prefixes. The checker resolves each imported root-package module's origin and rejects unexpected project modules, imports of excluded modules into claimed ones, and unknown ownership (unexpected-project-module and related subreasons).\n\nThe impact depends on the subreason. A forbidden import or a module outside every manifested library (unexpected-project-module) is a violation (lake lint exit 1 unless the same run also has an incomplete finding). A configured module that was omitted or not freshly built, or a declaration attributed outside the claimed surface, is incomplete evidence (INCOMPLETE, lake lint exit 3).\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL2004: Owned coverage must match the exact Lake inventory","header":"What triggers it","id":"/rules/PL2004/#PL2004-trigger"},"/rules/PL4002/#PL4002-trigger":{"contents":"Each positive fence is elaborated exactly as printed, with no inserted imports or wrappers, against a fresh build of the claimed libraries. It must be warning-free, pass checked admission, and pass the declaration and axiom rules under Standard-Logical. The fence failure is reported here together with the underlying finding (for example PL1001 for an axiom in the example).\n\nA fence that fails without a source diagnostic (for example a worker that stopped before completing) is reported as INCOMPLETE, not as a violation.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL4002: Positive examples require warning-free elaboration and admission","header":"What triggers it","id":"/rules/PL4002/#PL4002-trigger"},"/rules/PL5001/#PL5001-trigger":{"contents":"When a claimed module finishes elaborating, the checker asks Lean for its module documentation. A module without any is rejected with applicability module-documentation. Empty modules are included.\n\n","context":"Plumb for Lean rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009PL5001: Claimed modules require module documentation","header":"What triggers it","id":"/rules/PL5001/#PL5001-trigger"}});